    function javaTrim(s) {
        return WIR.javaText.stringTrim(s);
    }

    /**
     * ServerMetricsMapper.asNumber: a JSON number, or text Java parses as a double — trimmed —
     * and never NaN or an infinity, on either arm (an infinite fail band cannot be breached, which
     * is a silent PASS). Null for anything else: a boolean, an object, a unit suffix, "".
     *
     * <p>The text arm is Double.parseDouble's grammar, WIR.javaText.parseDouble: parseFloat read
     * "50ms" as 50 and Number read "" as 0, both numbers asNumber refuses, so a refused band was
     * judged here. This module kept its own copy of the grammar until the Asserts tab's percentile
     * reader needed the same one (RB8); the copy could round a hex float twice.
     */
